    "created_at": "2016-09-23T08:45:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-23T08:45:43Z",
    "body": "It looks like WebKit managed to simplify this a bit but the port to Blink was reverted:\nhttp://trac.webkit.org/changeset/149652\nhttps://crrev.com/384390341c5e98ae127e02325fb53df1997474e7\nhttps://crrev.com/4c86be9cd7d7f12109227febd895d72357a4554d\n\nAnyway, in Blink, `shouldRegisterAsNamedItem()` returns true for `embed`, `form`, `img` and `object`, while `shouldRegisterAsExtraNamedItem()`  returns true for `img` and `object`. `a`, `area` and `frameset` aren't special.\n\n@cdumez, can you prepare a web-platform-tests PR to test that the `name` attribute on  _don't_ do anything special and check if that would pass on all engines? Then we can change the spec and tests together. The spec PR would be easy too, if you're feeling up to it.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
